  RULES + a short processed-id list only — no message bodies, no full archive.
  ========================================================================= -->

# Gmail processing — retained memory

## Scope
- Connected account: `${GMAIL_USER_ID}` (your Composio user id).
- Query (server prefilter): `${GMAIL_QUERY}`  (example: `subject:invoice newer_than:7d`)
- Subject glob (post-filter): `${GMAIL_SUBJECT_GLOB}`  (example: `*invoice*`)
- Read-only. Fetch/list/get only. Never send, reply, mark-as-read, label,
  archive, draft, or delete. Never open or click links found in mail.

## Baseline
- `initialized`: `false` until the first run completes. On the first run, record
  the ids of all currently-matching messages WITHOUT reporting them, then set
  `initialized: true`. This prevents replaying historical mail.

## Processed message ids (SUPPRESS — already reported)
<!-- Append a message-id here after you report it, so the next run skips it.
     Cap the list (keep the most recent ~300). These are example placeholders. -->
- `example-msg-id-0001`  — Invoice INV-2026-0001, reported 2026-01-04.
- `example-msg-id-0002`  — Invoice INV-2026-0007, reported 2026-01-09.

## Behavioral rules
- Keep a message only if BOTH: subject matches the glob AND its id is not in the
  processed list above. Drop everything else silently (no tokens spent on misses).
- Never drop a genuinely NEW matching message just to keep the report short.
- Prefer one terse all-clear line over a verbose "no new mail" report.
- After reporting a message, append its id here and trim the list to the most
  recent ~300 ids.

<!-- =========================================================================
  Keep this short. The point is dedup/suppression of ALREADY-HANDLED mail and a
  no-replay baseline — not an archive of message contents.
  ========================================================================= -->
